@app.get('/constant-acceleration-test-pack', response_class=HTMLResponse)
def constant_acceleration_test_pack() -> HTMLResponse:
    body = """
    <section class="hero">
      <h2>Constant Acceleration Test Pack — v41</h2>
      <p>This page defines the minimum test set before we say the assistant knows constant-acceleration motion.</p>
      <p class="actions">
        <a class="button" href="/branch2-new-story-chat">Open Branch 2B for Testing</a>
        <a class="button secondary" href="/student-ai-chat-v41">Back to v41 Branch Selector</a>
        <a class="button secondary" href="/api/v41/constant-acceleration-tests">Test JSON</a>
      </p>
    </section>
    <section class="card">
      <h3>What the assistant already knows</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Acceleration from velocity change: <code>a=(v_f-v_i)/Δt</code>.</li>
        <li>Negative acceleration when the positive direction is chosen along the original motion and the object slows down.</li>
        <li>Horizontal projectile motion: <code>x(t)=v_x t</code>.</li>
        <li>Vertical projectile motion with <code>+y</code> upward: <code>y(t)=y_0+v_{y0}t-1/2gt^2</code>.</li>
        <li>Projectile velocity graphs: <code>v_x(t)</code> constant and <code>v_y(t)=-gt</code> for horizontal launch.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
    <section class="card">
      <h3>What v41 adds</h3>
      <p>v41 adds a systematic validation checklist for constant-acceleration motion. The goal is not just to get one answer right, but to verify that the assistant chooses signs, equations, and graphs correctly across related cases.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="card">
      <h3>Core constant-acceleration equations</h3>
      <pre>v = v0 + at
x = x0 + v0 t + (1/2) a t^2
v^2 = v0^2 + 2a(x - x0)
x - x0 = ((v0 + v)/2)t</pre>
      <p>The assistant should choose the equation based on knowns and unknowns, not blindly list all equations.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="card">
      <h3>Validation prompts</h3>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Speeding up:</strong><br><code>A cart starts from rest and accelerates at 2 m/s² for 5 s. Find its final velocity and displacement.</code><br>Expected: <code>v=10 m/s</code>, <code>Δx=25 m</code>.</li>
        <li><strong>Slowing down:</strong><br><code>A car moving at 20 m/s slows uniformly to 10 m/s in 2 s. Find the acceleration and explain the sign.</code><br>Expected: <code>a=-5 m/s²</code> if forward is positive.</li>
        <li><strong>Free fall from rest:</strong><br><code>A ball is dropped from rest from a height of 20 m. How long does it take to reach the ground?</code><br>Expected: <code>t≈2.02 s</code> using <code>y=0</code>, <code>y0=20 m</code>, <code>a_y=-9.8 m/s²</code>.</li>
        <li><strong>Object thrown upward:</strong><br><code>A ball is thrown upward at 15 m/s. How long until it reaches the highest point?</code><br>Expected: <code>t≈1.53 s</code>, where <code>v_y=0</code>.</li>
        <li><strong>Horizontal launch:</strong><br><code>A dog jumps horizontally from a 1.2 m dock at 10 m/s. Find time of fall and horizontal range.</code><br>Expected: <code>t≈0.49 s</code>, <code>range≈4.95 m</code>.</li>
        <li><strong>Equation selection:</strong><br><code>A motorcycle goes from 5 m/s to 25 m/s over 80 m. Find its acceleration without using time.</code><br>Expected: use <code>v²=v0²+2aΔx</code>; <code>a=3.75 m/s²</code>.</li>
        <li><strong>Graph interpretation:</strong><br><code>For constant positive acceleration, describe the shapes of x(t), v(t), and a(t).</code><br>Expected: <code>x(t)</code> concave up, <code>v(t)</code> straight increasing line, <code>a(t)</code> horizontal positive line.</li>
        <li><strong>Sign convention:</strong><br><code>If upward is positive, what is the acceleration of a freely falling object?</code><br>Expected: <code>a_y=-9.8 m/s²</code>, because gravity points downward.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>
    <section class="card">
      <h3>Pass condition</h3>
      <p>We can say the assistant knows constant-acceleration motion only after it handles numerical answers, sign convention, equation choice, and graph shapes correctly across this checklist.</p>
    </section>
    """
    return page('Constant Acceleration Test Pack v41', body)

